    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d986">

                <pb facs="1149" n="953" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg953"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/7–2145: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 986<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied
                        Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">and
                        the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d986-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-21">July 21, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi>–184.
                    From Pauley and Clayton.</p>
                <p>In view of note presented by AmEmbassy
                    Moscow to Soviet [Government]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d986-f2"/> based on your July
                    18 [<hi rendition="#italic">17</hi>] telegraphed instructions re Spanish
                        situation,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d986-f3"/> believe it highly desirable to
                    repeat to Moscow your telegram 56, July 18, re Rumanian oil shares.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d986-f4"/> Also believe desirable to repeat to Moscow details of
                    Soviet negotiations re German property in Stockholm, both in case of Soviet
                    questions on note presented by Embassy. See no reason not to repeat telegram re
                    Rumanian oil shares to Bucharest.</p>
                <p>American delegation is presenting to conference its view that a declaration
                    should be issued by US, UK, USSR, and if possible
                    France, declaring German external assets subject to jurisdiction of powers
                    occupying Germany and of ACC, and naming
                    diplomatic representatives of occupying powers as agents for both.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d986-f5"/>
                    Rubin and Dubois here working on text of proposed vesting decree with view
                    to presenting decree to US Group CC for
                    presentation to ACC.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d986-f6"/>
                    ES comments being considered.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
